meta {
  name: A clean question
  type: http
  seq: 64
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timetables/{{timetableId}}/clash-check
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "rules": ["room"],
    "proposed": []
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.clear: eq true
  res.body.count: eq 0
}

docs {
  An empty proposal list checks the timetable against itself under one rule.
  It is clear because request 57 was refused: nothing that clashes was ever
  written, so the plan on disk is always consistent under the rules that were
  on when it was built. Narrowing rules is how a school that shares rooms with
  a neighbouring campus turns the room rule off without losing the teacher
  one.
}
